-# The DevTools Times
+# smallpt — The light playground
 
-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
+Kevin Beason’s open-source C++ path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. The Astro playground is served at `/` and `/index.html`.
 
+```sh
+pnpm install
+pnpm dev --host 0.0.0.0
+```
+
+Rendering happens entirely on the client in a module Web Worker. The renderer sends progressive RGBA frames to a canvas; no rendering server or cross-origin isolation is required. It renders automatically, and Randomize colors changes the two mirror/glass sphere tints and starts a fresh render. You can also adjust samples, resolution, and individual colors, reset the scene, expand the canvas, or save its current output as PNG.
+
+## Rebuild the C++ renderer
+
+The compiled JavaScript and `.wasm` are included in `public/renderer/`, so Emscripten is only needed when changing the C++ source. Built using Emscripten 6.0.1.
+
+```sh
+pnpm build:wasm
+```
+
+`renderer/smallpt-original.cpp` preserves the upstream source. `renderer/smallpt.cpp` keeps its ray/sphere intersections and Monte Carlo integrator, replaces the CLI/PPM output with a progressive RGBA interface, adds a depth bound for browser stack safety, and gives the room a sage palette. The two spheres retain their original mirror and glass materials. The bundled preview was generated using this adapted C++ renderer; live WebAssembly output replaces it after the first complete pass.
+
+## Build and check
 
 ```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
+pnpm check:renderer
+pnpm build
+pnpm start
 ```
 
-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+The command-line checks exercise the actual WebAssembly binary, verifying progressive sampling, pixel output, reproducible seeds, changed sphere colors, worker completion, and cancellation. No browser automation is used.
 
-## Tech Stack
+Original project: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/
 
-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+smallpt © 2006–2008 Kevin Beason, MIT License. The license is preserved in `renderer/LICENSE.txt` and distributed with the browser assets.
